{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/18901-spending-your-exp-on-attr-skill-merits-and-athanor-sounds-good-in-the-long-run","id":18901,"title":"Spending your exp on Attr/Skill/Merits and Athanor sounds good in the long run?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-26T20:07:21-08:00","id":18901,"title":"Spending your exp on Attr/Skill/Merits and Athanor sounds good in the long run?","content":"Okay so in the New Dawn you likely loose all your supernatural tricks, but if you spent all your exp on normal things like Attributes, Skills, and Merits as well as the Athanors then it sounds like you would be in a much better condition when you achieve the New Dawn compared to those who spent all their EXP on nasty supernatural tricks.<br /> <br /> I guess the reasoning is you should concentrate on what can best allow you to survive your pilgrimage as well as what can more easily provide clues to milestones.<br /> <br /> I don't have my books on me but does everyone keep traits beyond the human limit, or is that something you have to roll to keep? Either way even if it caps out at 5 it sounds like if a lot of people achieve the New Dawn after a long Pilgrimage they would pop up as extremely talented and gifted human beings, among the worlds finest in their specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T05:34:50-08:00","id":19108,"title":"","content":"Before the GMC update, Attributes that you bought up above 5 via Bestowments were the one thing you were able to keep if you succeed on the Crucible roll and attain the New Dawn, and yeah: ex-Prometheans tend to be exemplars in some aspect of humanity. Makes sense to me--they've been studying it for their entire existence. A Promethean who decides to develop human-only traits is probably getting pretty close to completing their Pilgrimage (though if they see this as a sort of shortcut, well, they probably have a lot longer way to go).<br /> <br /> In pre-GMC rules the lifting of the Attribute cap was balanced due to the increase in XP costs, which then prevented you from getting other cool stuff. In the new rules, though, everything has a flat Experience cost. I'm tempted to say that that particular part of Bestowments should be axed, but you're still just going to be increasing dice pools instead of getting cool new powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T17:05:20-08:00","id":21357,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s got nothing to do with Bestowments. If you have Azoth \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 or more, you can buy attributes up beyond five dots; if an Attribute exceeds five dots when you Redeem, you get to keep it. It\u2019s as simple as that. <br /> <br /> Spending Experience on traits that you\u2019ll retain once you become human is definitely a sign of a forward-thinking Promethean. Conversely, Vitriol can technically only be spent on Promethean-specific traits; so it\u2019s reasonable for a Promethean to devote hid Vitriol to acquiring Bestowments and Transmutations to help him on his Pilgrimage. Except\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026Except that Vitriol <i>can</i> be spent on Humanity, which translates into Morality when you Redeem; and once you\u2019ve acquired an Athanor, you gain the ability to spend Vitriol on two mortal traits particular to that Athanor. So: prioritize Azoth and Humanity until you can get an Athanor, then prioritize the Athanor Traits and Humanity until they\u2019re maxed out. Once Azoth, Humanity, and the Athanor Traits are maxed out, <i>then</i> start spending Vitriol on Bestowments and Transmutations, and/or bank it in your Athanor. <br /> <br /> Strictly from a utilitaran perspective, mind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T03:24:53-08:00","id":30880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/18901-spending-your-exp-on-attr-skill-merits-and-athanor-sounds-good-in-the-long-run?p=21357#post21357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s got nothing to do with Bestowments. If you have Azoth \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 or more, you can buy attributes up beyond five dots; if an Attribute exceeds five dots when you Redeem, you get to keep it. It\u2019s as simple as that.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I admit I did forget that you can go above the cap once you get to higher Azoth levels, Unholy Strength, Unholy Stamina, and Mesmerizing Appearance all remove the cap on their respective Attributes permanently (Mesmerizing Appearance even gives you two for one). The Uncanny Dexterity Transmutation also removes the cap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/18901-spending-your-exp-on-attr-skill-merits-and-athanor-sounds-good-in-the-long-run?p=21357#post21357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spending Experience on traits that you\u2019ll retain once you become human is definitely a sign of a forward-thinking Promethean. Conversely, Vitriol can technically only be spent on Promethean-specific traits; so it\u2019s reasonable for a Promethean to devote hid Vitriol to acquiring Bestowments and Transmutations to help him on his Pilgrimage. Except\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026Except that Vitriol <i>can</i> be spent on Humanity, which translates into Morality when you Redeem; and once you\u2019ve acquired an Athanor, you gain the ability to spend Vitriol on two mortal traits particular to that Athanor. So: prioritize Azoth and Humanity until you can get an Athanor, then prioritize the Athanor Traits and Humanity until they\u2019re maxed out. Once Azoth, Humanity, and the Athanor Traits are maxed out, <i>then</i> start spending Vitriol on Bestowments and Transmutations, and/or bank it in your Athanor.<br /> <br /> Strictly from a utilitaran perspective, mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a sound plan that you should absolutely try to tempt your players away from at every opportunity! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T16:32:10-08:00","id":34164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/18901-spending-your-exp-on-attr-skill-merits-and-athanor-sounds-good-in-the-long-run?p=30880#post30880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I admit I did forget that you can go above the cap once you get to higher Azoth levels, Unholy Strength, Unholy Stamina, and Mesmerizing Appearance all remove the cap on their respective Attributes permanently (Mesmerizing Appearance even gives you two for one). The Uncanny Dexterity Transmutation also removes the cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026 true enough. It makes me wonder what sorts of Transmutations and/or alternate Bestowments would be needed to unlock the caps for the remaining four attributes (Intelligence, Wits, Resolve, and Composure). Given their propensity toward cold curiosity, I could see the Nepri having an alternate \u201cUnholy Attribute\u201d Bestowment for Intelligence and/or Composure (I\u2019d lean toward Unholy Intellect), which would leave only the Ulgans without an \u201cUnholy Attribute\u201d Bestowment. Even there, I could see them maybe having something for perception (and Wits) in much the same way that Mesmerizing Appearance works for the Galeteids. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/18901-spending-your-exp-on-attr-skill-merits-and-athanor-sounds-good-in-the-long-run?p=30880#post30880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a sound plan that you should absolutely try to tempt your players away from at every opportunity! :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}